'''''Ophiopogon planiscapus''''' is a [[species]] of [[flowering plant]] in the [[Family (taxonomy)|family]] Asparagaceae. It is a small [[evergreen]] [[perennial plant|perennial]] growing to {{convert|20|cm|0|abbr=on}} tall by {{convert|30|cm|0|abbr=on}}wide.<ref name=RHSAZ>{{cite book|title=RHS A-Z encyclopedia of garden plants|year=2008|publisher=Dorling Kindersley|location=United Kingdom|isbn=978-1405332965|pages=1136}}</ref> It grows from short [[rhizomes]], and bears tufts of grasslike leaves, from which purple or white flowers emerge in racemes held on short stems above the leaves. It is [[native plant|native]] to Japan, where it grows on open and forested slopes.<ref name=EGF>''European Garden Flora'' vol. 1, p. 266</ref><ref name=WPG>''When Perennials Bloom: An Almanac for Planning and Planting'' by Tomasz Aniśko, p. 342</ref>

==Garden use==
The cultivar 'Kokuryu' ('''black mondo''') is grown as [[groundcover]], or as underplanting for larger shrubs. Its leaves turn from green to dark purple (black) and can grow to {{cvt|8|in|cm|abbr=on}} tall and {{cvt|1/4|in|cm|abbr=on}} wide. The pale lilac flowers are followed by black berries. It is also known as 'Black Dragon', 'Nigra' or 'Nigrescens'.<ref>{{cite web | url = https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/search-results?query=Ophiopogon%20planiscapus | title = ''Ohiopogon planiscapus'' | publisher = RHS | access-date = 23 February 2022}}</ref> It has received the [[Royal Horticultural Society]]'s [[Award of Garden Merit]].<ref>{{cite web | title = RHS Plant Selector - ''Ophiopogon planiscapus'' 'Kokuryu' |url = https://www.rhs.org.uk/Plants/377774/Ophiopogon-planiscapus-Kokuryu/Details | access-date = 23 February 2022}}</ref>

There are also two variegated forms called 'Little Tabby' and 'Silver Ribbon'. These are green with white borders around the leaves.<ref>{{Cite book | url = https://archive.org/details/isbn_9780881928877 | title = When perennials bloom : an almanac for planning and planting | last=Aniśko |first=Tomasz|date=2008|publisher=Timber Press|isbn=9780881928877|location=Portland|oclc=191846797|url-access=registration}}</ref>

==Propagation==
The plants spread by underground [[stolons]] with thick fleshy roots making fair sized colonies which can be separated by [[Division (horticulture)|division]] in the spring.
It also produces fruits with berries.

